# Commise Mobile — Expo environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.
# Or run `node scripts/fetch-secrets.mjs` to pull the Clerk publishable key from AWS.
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time; non-prefixed vars are build/CI-only.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — Clerk / IDP authentication
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Clerk publishable key (pk_test on sandbox/dev, pk_live on prod). Read by App.tsx at startup.
EXPO_PUBLIC_IDP_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your-publishable-key

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — API backend
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declared and validated in src/config/env.ts. There is NO in-code default: an absent or blank value is a
# startup failure, not a fallback. `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined at BUILD time, so a default is frozen into
# the shipped binary — and every default this replaced was an unsafe guess (`localhost` on a phone is the
# PHONE, and `https://api.commise.io` is a hostname nothing in this repo provisions).
#
# You normally do NOT need to set these locally: the committed `.env.development` supplies both localhost
# origins. Override them in .env.local for an emulator or a real device (see the notes below).
#
# The RECIPE API origin (no trailing /v1 — the typed clients add the path). On the Android emulator use
# http://10.0.2.2:3000 (10.0.2.2 is the host loopback); on iOS simulator http://localhost:3000 works. On a
# real DEVICE neither works — use your machine's LAN address, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:3000.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RECIPE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
# The IDENTITY API origin, serving /v1/users/me + /v1/accounts/me (viewer profile + subscription tier).
# Identity is a SEPARATE service on a SEPARATE host from recipe (sandbox/prod: identity.{stage} vs
# recipe.{stage}), so it needs its own origin — pointing it at the recipe origin 404s every profile fetch,
# which leaves the viewer id unresolved and hides owner-gated UI (edit/delete/clone-eligibility). It no
# longer falls back to the recipe origin: that fallback turned a missing setting into a broken screen.
# Local: run the identity service on :4000 and set http://localhost:4000 (emulator: http://10.0.2.2:4000).
EXPO_PUBLIC_IDENTITY_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — Stage marker (sandbox | pr-{N} | prod), surfaced for Sentry/env gating.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STAGE=sandbox

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Device / EAS builds — where a BINARY gets its endpoints (this file is not read there)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `eas.json` selects the source per profile, and it is not uniform, because the backends are not:
#
#   production — hardcoded literals (recipe.commise.app / identity.commise.app). Correct, because prod is a
#                single persistent deployment.
#   e2e        — hardcoded 10.0.2.2 loopbacks. The Maestro suite drives services on the CI runner.
#   preview    — NO literals; declares `environment: "preview"`, so EAS supplies them per build.
#
# `preview` has no literals because **every PR deploys its own recipe service** — only identity and
# packages/infra/global are shared and persistent — so there is no fixed non-prod recipe host to name. Set,
# per preview build:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_RECIPE_API_URL   = https://recipe-pr-{N}.commise.app   (THIS PR's service)
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_IDENTITY_API_URL = https://identity.sandbox.commise.app (shared, all PRs)
#
# It previously hardcoded `https://recipe.sandbox.commise.app`, a host that must never exist. Note that this
# would NOT have failed loudly: the `*.sandbox.commise.app` wildcard resolves to the shared ALB, which
# answers its default 404 — so every request would fail while the build looked correctly configured.
# tests/config/easProfiles.test.ts refuses that shape now.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — Sentry observability
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side DSN (exposed to the app via the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix)
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# Source-map upload credentials (CI / build only)
SENTRY_ORG=radicle-co
SENTRY_PROJECT=commise-mobile
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
